#: ../../../devel/ssi.rst:3
msgid "SSI devices and SPI flash models"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devel/ssi.rst:5
msgid ""
"QEMU's Synchronous Serial Interface (SSI) bus models the full-duplex "
"transfer of words between a controller and one selected peripheral. Most SPI "
"flash models, including ``m25p80``, are attached to controllers through this "
"bus."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devel/ssi.rst:9
msgid ""
"This page documents the expected boundary between a controller model and a "
"flash model for SPI fast-read dummy cycles. The boundary is important "
"because many real controllers expose dummy-cycle configuration in registers, "
"while the flash model observes only the byte stream delivered through "
"``ssi_transfer()``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devel/ssi.rst:15
msgid "SSI transfer granularity"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devel/ssi.rst:17
msgid ""
"``ssi_transfer()`` transfers one SSI word. Flash models that implement "
"common SPI NOR command streams usually consume one 8-bit word at a time:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devel/ssi.rst:20
msgid "command opcode;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devel/ssi.rst:21
msgid "address bytes;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devel/ssi.rst:22
msgid "optional mode or continuous-read bytes;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devel/ssi.rst:23
msgid "dummy bytes;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devel/ssi.rst:24
msgid "data bytes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devel/ssi.rst:26
msgid ""
"The SSI core does not model individual clock edges or the number of active "
"SPI data lines. If a real transaction has a dummy phase expressed in clock "
"cycles, the device model that generates transfers on the SSI bus must "
"represent that phase as a number of dummy byte transfers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devel/ssi.rst:32
msgid "Flash model responsibilities"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devel/ssi.rst:34
msgid "A SPI flash model owns the command semantics for the flash device:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devel/ssi.rst:36
msgid "which opcodes are recognized;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devel/ssi.rst:37
msgid "how many address bytes are required;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devel/ssi.rst:38
msgid "whether a command has mode bytes;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devel/ssi.rst:39
msgid "how many dummy bytes must be consumed before data can be returned;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devel/ssi.rst:40
msgid "manufacturer-specific differences in fast-read command behavior."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devel/ssi.rst:42
msgid ""
"For the ``m25p80`` model, ``needed_bytes`` is a byte count. It must not "
"store raw dummy cycles. When a flash datasheet describes the dummy phase in "
"cycles, the flash model converts the cycles to bytes using the bus width "
"used for the dummy phase::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devel/ssi.rst:47
msgid "dummy_bytes = DIV_ROUND_UP(dummy_cycles * dummy_bus_width, 8)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devel/ssi.rst:49
msgid ""
"For SPI NOR fast-read commands modeled by ``m25p80``, the dummy phase "
"follows the address phase width. For example, output-only dual and quad read "
"commands such as DOR and QOR use one line for command, address, and dummy "
"phases, then use two or four lines only for the data phase. Dual I/O and "
"Quad I/O commands such as DIOR and QIOR use the wider bus for both address "
"and dummy phases."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devel/ssi.rst:55
msgid ""
"If the exact dummy phase cannot be represented as a whole number of SSI byte "
"transfers, the model should round up and log the limitation instead of "
"silently treating cycles as bytes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devel/ssi.rst:60
msgid "Controller model responsibilities"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devel/ssi.rst:62
msgid "A controller model owns the behavior of the controller hardware:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devel/ssi.rst:64
msgid ""
"how guest-visible registers select command, address width, bus width, and "
"dummy-cycle count;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devel/ssi.rst:66
msgid "whether the guest supplies dummy bytes in a transmit FIFO;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devel/ssi.rst:67
msgid ""
"whether the controller itself generates the dummy phase for a memory-mapped, "
"direct-read, or other automatic transfer mode;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devel/ssi.rst:69
msgid "how chip-select state changes around controller-generated transfers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devel/ssi.rst:71
msgid ""
"When guest software writes dummy bytes into a transmit FIFO or manual "
"transfer path, the controller should pass those bytes to ``ssi_transfer()`` "
"like any other guest-provided byte. It should not add more dummy transfers "
"on behalf of the flash."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devel/ssi.rst:76
msgid ""
"When hardware registers instruct the controller to generate a dummy phase, "
"the controller must emit dummy byte transfers before data transfers reach "
"the flash model. The controller should convert the configured cycle count "
"using the bus width that the controller uses during the dummy phase. For "
"example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devel/ssi.rst:81
msgid "8 dummy cycles on a single data line become 1 dummy byte;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devel/ssi.rst:82
msgid "8 dummy cycles on two data lines become 2 dummy bytes;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devel/ssi.rst:83
msgid "8 dummy cycles on four data lines become 4 dummy bytes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devel/ssi.rst:85
msgid ""
"The controller should not duplicate flash-specific opcode tables merely to "
"guess which commands need dummy cycles. In automatic modes the controller "
"already has enough hardware configuration to know whether it must generate a "
"dummy phase. In manual modes the guest-provided byte stream is authoritative."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devel/ssi.rst:91
msgid "Avoiding double counting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devel/ssi.rst:93
msgid ""
"Exactly one side should generate each dummy byte transfer seen by the flash:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devel/ssi.rst:95
msgid ""
"If the guest sends dummy bytes through the controller, the controller "
"forwards them and the flash consumes them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devel/ssi.rst:97
msgid ""
"If the guest programs a controller dummy-cycle register, the controller "
"converts those cycles to dummy byte transfers and the flash consumes them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devel/ssi.rst:99
msgid ""
"The flash may know that a command requires dummy bytes, but it does not "
"create transfers on the SSI bus."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devel/ssi.rst:102
msgid ""
"Do not implement controller-side snooping that watches manual-mode opcode "
"streams and injects extra dummy transfers based on flash opcodes. That mixes "
"flash command semantics into the controller and is fragile when flash models "
"gain correct dummy-byte accounting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devel/ssi.rst:108
msgid "Examples in the tree"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devel/ssi.rst:110
msgid "The following models illustrate the boundary:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devel/ssi.rst:112
msgid ""
"``hw/block/m25p80.c`` keeps fast-read dummy requirements as byte counts in "
"``needed_bytes``. Manufacturer-specific helpers convert datasheet dummy "
"cycles to the byte stream expected by the model."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devel/ssi.rst:115
msgid ""
"``hw/ssi/aspeed_smc.c`` generates dummy byte transfers for direct fast-read "
"mode from controller registers, but manual user-mode writes are forwarded as "
"guest-provided bytes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devel/ssi.rst:118
msgid ""
"``hw/ssi/npcm7xx_fiu.c`` converts the direct-read dummy configuration to the "
"number of dummy byte transfers sent before reading data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devel/ssi.rst:122
msgid "Review checklist"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devel/ssi.rst:124
msgid "When adding or changing a SPI flash controller or flash model, check:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devel/ssi.rst:126
msgid ""
"Are dummy counts stored in byte units when they drive flash state machines?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devel/ssi.rst:127
msgid ""
"If a hardware register stores cycles, is the conversion to bytes based on "
"the bus width of the dummy phase?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devel/ssi.rst:129
msgid ""
"Are manual guest-provided dummy bytes forwarded without extra injection?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devel/ssi.rst:130
msgid ""
"Are automatic controller-generated dummy phases modeled by the controller?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devel/ssi.rst:131
msgid ""
"Is flash-specific opcode knowledge kept in the flash model rather than "
"copied into controller snooping paths?"
msgstr ""
